    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11960" root="دب" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا بِالدَّارِ دُبِّىٌّ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبِّىٌّ</span> <i>There is not in the
house any one:</i> (S, M, * K:) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُبِّىٌّ</span> being from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبَبْتُ</span>; i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْ يَدِبُّ</span>; and it is not used in any
but a negative phrase. (Ks, S.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبِّيجٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبِّيحٌ</span>.]

